mount
    Mount a specific package variant to global/system scope so that it is available to all packages installed on host os

    viator mount "pkg+variant"

    Example:
        $ sudo viator mount "icu.lama:helloworld:version+customFeature1+avx512"
        mount helloworld 1.0 (variant AABBCCDDEE)
          link  /usr/bin/helloworld -> ~/.viator/bin/.../helloworld
          link  /usr/bin/meow -> ~/.viator/bin/.../meow
        $ helloworld
        world hello!

    Interactive + custom path Example:
        $ sudo viator mount "..." --at /usr/local --interactive
        mount helloworld 1.0 (variant AABBCCDDEE)
        File ~/.viator/bin/.../helloworld
          (A)uto, (R)ename, (S)kip,
          Action: R
          Rename: hw
        File ~/.viator/bin/.../meow
          (A)uto, (R)ename, (S)kip,
          Action: S


          link  /usr/local/bin/hw -> ~/.viator/bin/.../helloworld
          skip  ~/.viator/bin/.../meow
        $ hw
        world hello!
        $ meow
        meow: command not found
